From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] login: PAM policy with pam_unix in place of pam_opendirectory

login's /etc/pam.d/login and login.term authenticate and manage accounts
through pam_opendirectory, and try pam_krb5, pam_ntlm and pam_mount: all
need closed frameworks (OpenDirectory, CoreFoundation, Heimdal, GSS, NetFS),
and OpenPAM fails the whole policy when a module doesn't load. NeoDarwin's
password module is OpenPAM's pam_unix (crypt(3) against /etc/master.passwd);
nullok lets root's empty password log in, on a secure terminal only (patch
0001). pam_launchd, which moves the session into a per-user launchd, is left
out: NeoDarwin's launchd runs none. pam_uwtmp becomes optional: on a
read-only root (before launchctl remounts it read-write, or under the test
PID 1 that runs getty itself) it can't write utmpx, and login's non-PAM
path ignored that failure too (docs/base/session.md, "PAM").

--- a/login/pam.d/login
+++ b/login/pam.d/login
@@ -1,11 +1,6 @@
 # login: auth account password session
-auth       optional       pam_krb5.so use_kcminit
-auth       optional       pam_ntlm.so try_first_pass
-auth       optional       pam_mount.so try_first_pass
-auth       required       pam_opendirectory.so try_first_pass
+auth       required       pam_unix.so nullok
 account    required       pam_nologin.so
-account    required       pam_opendirectory.so
-password   required       pam_opendirectory.so
-session    required       pam_launchd.so
-session    required       pam_uwtmp.so
-session    optional       pam_mount.so
+account    required       pam_unix.so
+password   required       pam_unix.so
+session    optional       pam_uwtmp.so
--- a/login/pam.d/login.term
+++ b/login/pam.d/login.term
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
 # login: account session
 account    required       pam_nologin.so
-account    required       pam_opendirectory.so
-session    required       pam_uwtmp.so
+account    required       pam_unix.so
+session    optional       pam_uwtmp.so
